      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Combined percutaneous coronary and peripheral intervention in patients with coronary and peripheral vascular disease can be time and cost saving. Despite the potential benefit, such hybrid procedures have been rarely reported. We report two cases of hybrid peripheral and coronary intervention that were performed at our institution with excellent outcomes. This is followed by a review of the literature."},
